# Pin classes: who may move the pins (image refs, pkg==version, commits, *_TAG/
# *_VERSION/*_IMAGE/... assignments) in each path. hack/pin-classes reads this file,
# hack/pin-guard enforces it on every PR and push to main, and `scripts/images-lock
# repin` leaves ledger and historical paths alone.
#
#   <glob> ours|eat-stock|historical [reason]
#   <glob> ledger <rows csv> amend=<aliases csv> [reason]
#   historical-ref <path> <exact string>
#
# First match wins; * also matches /. A path no line matches is ours, except a file
# under bench/ or oracle/ that holds a pin: hack/pin-classes coverage fails on it.
#
# ours        k3d-gpu's own pins: always the latest stable release.
# eat-stock   tracks Intel EAT's latest release (intel/enterprise-agent-toolkit); reviewed.
# ledger      a ledger row's runner or records. While any listed row is PENDING in the
#             EXPERIMENTS.md Hypotheses table the path is an arm: a pin changes only
#             with a dated amendment in the same diff whose heading names a PENDING
#             listed row or an alias ("### <alias> amendment <ID>: <title> (YYYY-MM-DD)").
#             Once a listed row has a verdict and none is PENDING it is historical.
# historical  a finished run's record: never modified, deleted or renamed.
# historical-ref  a finished run's pin inside a live runner: it keeps occurring as
#             often as it does.

# --- EAT stock: what Intel's Enterprise Agent Toolkit ships --------------------------
